= Unpacking Your FujiNet Cartridge

== Introduction

Welcome to the wonderful world of the FujiNet cartridge for the EMERSON
ARCADIA-2001. Your micro-computer was made in 1982 to play the cartridges
at your Emerson dealer. With FujiNet it can also play games kept on the
Internet, on a memory card, or on a computer in your home -- and play some of
them against people far away. We suggest that you read this Owner’s Manual
before setting it up.

== What Is Included

When you take the FujiNet cartridge from its box, you will have:

- The FujiNet cartridge
- This Owner’s Manual

#fig-hero

The FujiNet cartridge goes in the cartridge slot like any other game. Inside
it is a complete network adapter: a WiFi radio, a memory-card reader and two
small computers of its own.

== What You Also Need

- *An EMERSON ARCADIA-2001* (model ADV-1), with its two hand controllers.
  FujiNet is made for the *NTSC* (North American) console and television
  sets. The Arcadia was also sold under many other names in other
  countries; FujiNet has not yet been tried in those.
- *Your WiFi network’s name and password.* FujiNet uses the 2.4 GHz band,
  which nearly every home router offers.

You may also want, though you do not need them to start:

- *A microSD memory card*, formatted FAT32 (most cards come that way), to
  keep games on.
- *A USB-C phone charger and cable*, for extra power. We recommend one;
  see Section 4.

#note[FujiNet makes no changes to your console. Take the cartridge out and
your ARCADIA-2001 is exactly as it was.]
